
# --- GOLDEN FIXTURE (see docs/guests/redhat62.md) ---
# Scene: Red Hat Linux 6.2 GNOME 1.0.55 desktop under Enlightenment, logged in
# as the unprivileged `gallery` user via the inittab startx respawn, 1024x768x16
# on cirrus (XF86_SVGA, Chipset clgd5446, Option no_bitblt). Two windows open:
# the GNOME Help Browser on "Red Hat Online Help" (toc:) and the GNOME file
# manager on /home/gallery; pointer parked at (512,620) on the help page.
# Baked 2026-09-03 03:18:53 UTC on the smoke rig, ACCEL=kvm -cpu host, UP
# kernel 2.2.14-5.0 (LILO default linux-up), hdparm -d1 active (using_dma=1).
# qemu-img snapshot -l: ID 1 golden VM_SIZE 86.4 MiB VM_CLOCK 0000:03:39.425.
# Restore-proven the same minute: loadvm golden + cont -> desktop, XWarpPointer
# (300,650) read back by XQueryPointer and seen on the framebuffer.
SH_RESET_MODE=loadvm
SH_GOLDEN_SNAPSHOT=golden
SH_RESET_MONITOR=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/redhat62/reset-hmp.sock
SH_FIXTURE_DESC="Red Hat Linux 6.2 GNOME desktop at 1024x768 as gallery, on the retronet: Netscape 4.72 on search.retronet and Gaim 0.59.9 signed in as UIN 18100 with HiveBot in the list; x11warp pointer through the guest X server"
SH_BASE_BACKUP=/data/gallery-guests/RedHat62/redhat62.qcow2.bak-pre-golden

# --- RETRONET (2026-09-03): web + ICQ planes ---
# The golden was RE-BAKED for the retronet join, on the new device set and after
# a COLD BOOT (not a savevm over a running restore): 2026-09-03 08:52:21 UTC,
# qemu-img snapshot -l ID 1 golden VM_SIZE 80.5 MiB VM_CLOCK 0000:02:11.960.
# Scene: Netscape Communicator 4.72 on http://search.retronet/ (the corpus
# search, seamless - no proxy, wildcard DNS -> the gateway :80 origin), the Gaim
# 0.59.9 buddy list showing HiveBot from the server-side SSI roster (signed in
# as UIN 18100), plus the GNOME Help Browser and gmc on /home/gallery. The whole
# scene is reproduced by a cold boot from ~gallery/.Xclients, so the golden is
# cold-bootable and not a snapshot of hand-arranged state.
# SECOND NIC: ne2k_pci on the bridged tap redhat62rn0 (vmbr-rn), static
# 10.99.0.33/24, DNS 10.99.0.2, NO default route on either NIC; guard chain
# REDHAT62RN-IN. The SLIRP NIC now carries restrict=on and eth0 is static
# 10.0.2.15/24, so nothing on the SLIRP side offers the guest a route - the
# forward 127.0.0.1:6081 -> 10.0.2.15:6000 still works and is the ONLY thing
# that NIC is for. Both NICs share guest IRQ 11 and both work.
# Details, proofs and traps: docs/lab/retronet/STATION-redhat62.md

# --- POINTER: ABSOLUTE THROUGH THE GUEST'S OWN X SERVER (x11warp) ---
# XFree86 3.3.6 listens on TCP :6000; the launcher forwards 127.0.0.1:6081 ->
# 10.0.2.15:6000 (loopback-only). /etc/X0.hosts in the golden grants 10.0.2.2.
# Buttons and keys ride the QEMU PS/2 path; the sink confirms each warp with
# XQueryPointer before an edge passes. Dead at the console/boot (BackendDown,
# motion dropped, counted) — the loadvm golden always restores a running X.
SH_INPUT_BACKEND=x11warp
SH_X11WARP_DISPLAY=127.0.0.1:81
SH_CURSOR_SCALE=1.0
SH_X11WARP_TRACE=off
